voxtype (1.1.1-0oaxaca1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Voxtype 1.1.1 (voxtype_1.1.1-1_amd64.deb, SHA-256 matching GitHub's
    digest), a fix release. VOXTYPE_VULKAN_DEVICE=nvidia, which the
    Dictation installer sets on laptops with an NVIDIA GPU, now moves
    Whisper to the NVIDIA GPU: 1.1.0 selected it and then initialized
    device 0, the integrated GPU, anyway. A daemon started at login waits
    for the GPU's render node before loading the model, instead of falling
    back to the CPU. Also: quiet microphones no longer lose short
    dictations, clipboard output no longer opens every input device, and
    voxtype's own config edits keep the file valid. The release's files
    are the same as 1.1.0's, so the package keeps the same ones.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:59:00 -0500

voxtype (1.1.0-0oaxaca1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Voxtype 1.1.0 for Oaxaca, from Voxtype's own release package
    (voxtype_1.1.0-1_amd64.deb), without its ONNX GPU builds (CUDA 12,
    CUDA 13, MIGraphX), which need runtimes the image does not have.
    Omarchy v4.0.4 installs Voxtype from the AUR; Ubuntu's archive
    has none.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0500
